c PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Spike: 15:00 of the second half, 11-13 down, 4 raids each left against the village's best raider. Two points is a lot in 8 raids: you need one stop and steady touches, and a second touch only when the gap beside your first is a rookie. Win by 1.","mechanics":["hand touch","dash home","struggle (pull-away)","ankle hold","thigh hold","comeback"],"optimal":null,"branching":9,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":11,"grid":"[Full Match · boss · Ch1 Village Mat] OPP MAT: o T T o T T o · grip 0.60 · KEY: o rookie, T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: alternate raids 00:00→12:00 (~17 raids in all, ~9 each, half-time swap at 06:00)\nMY MOVES: hand walk dash pull | DEFENCE: ankle thigh hold\nCPU RAIDER \"Bholu, the greedy captain\": s 0.50 · Easy · touches hand/toe · home dash · up to 2 touches · personality: goes for all 2 touches 80% of raids\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1o:h19 2T:h40 3T:h40 4o:h31 5T:h40 6T:h40 7o:h19 | home after 1 touch: walk 47%, dash 21% | after 2: walk 57%, dash 27% | if held: pull 42%\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 20/thigh 52; toe: ankle 53/thigh 19 | vs his way home — dash: ankle 34/thigh 18 | his touch lands 82% if untackled\nGOAL: win by 1+ | STARS: Win by 3; Win by 6\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 38/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 81/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him, but a Rusher standing NEXT to the kicked man charges the turned back — k = Kick held %, '(lands N)' = the Kick's landing chance); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Chapter boss and the first whole match, kept short: the Village Final as a mini-Blitz of 2x6 game minutes (~17 raids in all) with a half-time swap. Their captain Bholu has a personality you can read: he is greedy — he goes for two touches on 8 raids in 10 and always Dashes home. Aha: his second touch and his Dash are your chances — tackle his next target with the cover, or Ankle his Dash home; on your raids, raid the rookie gaps and Dash past the T's. Win the match.","mechanics":["hand touch","dash home","struggle (pull-away)","ankle hold","thigh hold","cover position","full match"],"optimal":null,"branching":9,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":12,"grid":"[Raid Puzzle · teach · Ch2 District Cup] OPP MAT: T T T T T T T · grip 0.18 · KEY: T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you raid 4x\nMY MOVES: hand toe walk dash pull\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1T:h14/t2 2T:h18/t3 3T:h18/t3 4T:h18/t3 5T:h18/t3 6T:h18/t3 7T:h14/t2 | home after 1 touch: walk 27%, dash 10% | after 2: walk 34%, dash 13% | if held: pull 47%\nGOAL: score 3 | FAIL: raider out 2x | STARS: Never get caught; Win within 3 raids\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 40/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 94/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him, but a Rusher standing NEXT to the kicked man charges the turned back — k = Kick held %, '(lands N)' = the Kick's landing chance); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTE