). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Twist: Ankle-catchers (A) on both corners and slot 3 wait for your Toe Touch, the T's wait for your Hand. The READ row shows the counter for each slot: Hand on an A, Toe on a T — and slot 2, a T between two A's, is the one to avoid with both. Aha: every defender has a counter. 4 points in 5 raids.","mechanics":["toe touch","hand touch","dash home","thigh-holders","ankle-catchers"],"optimal":null,"branching":16,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":14,"grid":"[Raid Puzzle · teach · Ch2 District Cup] OPP MAT: A o T T T T o · grip 0.35 · KEY: A ankle-catcher (Toe/hop/Dubki risky), o rookie, T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you raid 4x\nMY MOVES: hand walk dubki pull\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1A:h4 2o:h13 3T:h26 4T:h32 5T:h32 6T:h26 7o:h12 | home after 1 touch: walk 32%, dubki 17% | after 2: walk 40%, dubki 22% | if held: pull 45%\nGOAL: score 3, 1x lowMove | FAIL: raider out 2x | STARS: Score with Dubki twice; Never get caught\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 38/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 84/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him, but a Rusher standing NEXT to the kicked man charges the turned back — k = Kick held %, '(lands N)' = the Kick's landing chance); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Teach the Dubki ALONE (no Toe, no Dash, no wall, no bonus): four Thigh-holders in the middle reach for anyone walking home, and the Dubki ducks under a Thigh-holder's reach (READ after a touch: walk ~32% held, Dubki ~17%). One defender reads it: the Ankle-catcher on the left corner — and he is also the safest touch on the mat (Hand on the A ~4%). Aha: the Dubki is the way home under a reach — and it gets cleaner still once the corner Ankle-catcher is tagged out. Score 3 in 4 raids, at least one point coming home on a Dubki.","mechanics":["dubki","hand touch","thigh-holders","ankle-catchers"],"optimal":null,"branching":9,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":15,"grid":"[Defend Stand · teach · Ch2 District Cup] OPP MAT: o o o o o o o · grip 1.00 · KEY: o rookie\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you defend 5 CPU raids\nMY MOVES: hand toe walk dash dubki pull | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block hold\nCPU RAIDER \"District sprinter\": s 0.23 · Easy · touches hand/toe · home walk/dash · up to 1 touch\nBLOCK WINDOW: ×1.15 (wider timing for the teaching unit)\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 25/thigh 64; toe: ankle 65/thigh 23 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 28/thigh 49/block 41; dash: ankle 45/thigh 24/block 77 | his touch lands 76% if untackled\nGOAL: stop 3 raids | FAIL: opp scores > 5 | STARS: Win within his first 4 raids; Concede at most 2\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 38/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 90/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him, but a Rusher standing NEXT to the kicked man charges the turned back — k = Kick held %, '(lands N)' = the Kick's landing chance); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Teach the Block: the district sprinter telegraphs his way home — mostly a Dash, sometimes a walk. Against a Dash, let the touch go and form the Block on the midline (its timing window is a little wider in this first lesson, READ); against a walk the Block is weak and the Thigh Hold is the stop. Aha: defend the way home, not the touch — and read WHICH way home before you build the wall. Stop 3 of 5.","mechanics":["block (defensive wall)","ankle hold","thigh hold","return tackle"],"optimal":6,"branching":7,"trap":0,"explored":19896},{"n":16,"grid":"[Match · teach · Ch2 District Cup] OPP MAT: T T T A A A T · grip 0.84 · KEY: T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky), A ankle-catcher (Toe/hop/Dubki risky)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: alternate: 4 raids / 4 defences · start score 8-7 · empty raids 1/0\nMY MOVES: hand toe walk dash pull | DEFENCE: ankle thigh hold\nCPU RAIDER \"District raider\": s 0.45 · Easy · touches hand/toe · home walk · up to 1 touch\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1T:h50/t10 2T:h60/t13 3T:h51/t28 4A:h27/t52 5A:h11/t60 6A:h27/t52 7T:h39/t26 | home after 1 touch: walk 63%, dash 30% | after 2: walk 73%, dash 38% | if held: pull 40%\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 21/thigh 54; toe: ankle 56/thigh 20 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 23/thigh 39 | his touch lands 81% if untackled\nGOAL: win by 1+ | STARS: Exactly one empty raid; Never get caught\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 38/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 80/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him, but a Rusher standing NEXT to the kicked man charges the turned back — k = Kick held %, '(lands N)' = the Kick's landing chance); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Teach the empty-raid counter: you lead 8-7, already on 1 empty raid, and their mat is all hard — three Thigh-holders on the left, three Ankle-catchers on the right, a T on the far corner, no rookie anywhere. Each block has ONE counter touch and it is far safer than the wrong one (READ: Toe on a T inside the T block ~10-13% vs Hand ~50-60%; Hand on the A in the middle of the A block ~11% vs Toe ~60%); the men where the blocks meet are dangerous both ways. A caught raid hands them the point and the lead, an empty raid (walk home without touching) is free while you lead — but the THIRD empty in a row is Do-or-Die, so you get exactly one free one. Aha: spend the one patient empty raid, then touch the INSIDE of a block with its counter move. 4 raids each; finish ahead. The 3-star play is exactly one empty raid.","mechanics":["empty-raid counter","toe touch","hand touch","ankle-catchers","thigh-holders"],"optimal":null,"branching":16,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":17,"grid":"[Do-or-Die Drill · teach · Ch2 District Cup] OPP MAT: A o B B B o A · grip 0.28 · KEY: A ankle-catcher (Toe/hop/Dubki risky), o rookie, B blocker (Dash risky)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you raid 3x · empty raids 2/0\nMY MOVES: hand toe walk dash dubki pull\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1A:h3/t15 2o:h5/t11 3B:h6/t5 4B:h7/t6 5B:h6/t5 6o:h5/t11 7A:h3/t15 | home after 1 touch: walk 15%, dash 33%, dubki 21% | after 2: walk 19%, dash 41%, dubki 27% | if held: pull 47%\nGOAL: score 2, 1x dodWin | FAIL: raider out 2x | STARS: Score 3 points; Never get caught\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 39/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 83/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o 