rst raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"One lesson — survive the Do-or-Die: you are on two empty raids, so your FIRST raid must score or your raider is out. Ankle-catchers on the corners, a Blocker wall in the middle: the wall shuts the Dash home and the A's read the Dubki, so the safe way back is a plain walk, and the safe touch is a Hand on a corner A (READ). Win that raid and the trial is yours: score 2 in 3 raids. The greedy 3-point run (a second touch on a free raid after the Do-or-Die) is the star, never the goal. Aha: under Do-or-Die take the surest point, not the biggest.","mechanics":["do-or-die raid","toe touch","hand touch","ankle-catchers","blocker wall"],"optimal":null,"branching":17,"trap":0,"explored":40000},{"n":18,"grid":"[Raid Puzzle · teach · Ch2 District Cup] OPP MAT: o T T o T T o · grip 0.32 · KEY: o rookie, T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you raid 4x\nMY MOVES: hand toe bonus walk dash dubki pull\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1o:h11/t3 2T:h24/t5 3T:h24/t5 4o:h18/t5 5T:h24/t5 6T:h24/t5 7o:h11/t3 bonus:4 | home after 1 touch: walk 28%, dash 12%, dubki 7% | after 2: walk 36%, dash 16%, dubki 9% | if held: pull 46%\nGOAL: score 4, 2x bonus | FAIL: raider out 2x | STARS: Earn 3 bonus points; Never get caught\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 40/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 80/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him, but a Rusher standing NEXT to the kicked man charges the turned back — k = Kick held %, '(lands N)' = the Kick's landing chance); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Teach the bonus line: with 6+ defenders on the mat a hop over the bonus line scores 1 and puts nobody out. Rookie corners make the hop safe. Aha: bonus first — every touch puts a man out and below 6 the bonus line is closed. Earn 2 bonus points and 4 points total in 4 raids.","mechanics":["bonus line","toe touch","hand touch","dubki","thigh-holders"],"optimal":null,"branching":18,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":19,"grid":"[Revival Run · twist · Ch2 District Cup] OPP MAT: o o o o o o o · grip 0.39 · KEY: o rookie\nMY SIDE: o o - o o - o (5 on mat)\nFLOW: you defend 4 CPU raids\nMY MOVES: hand toe walk dash dubki pull | DEFENCE: ankle thigh hold\nCPU RAIDER \"District raider\": s 0.45 · Easy · touches hand/toe · home walk · up to 1 touch\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 21/thigh 54; toe: ankle 55/thigh 19 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 22/thigh 39 | his touch lands 81% if untackled\nGOAL: stop 2 raids | FAIL: opp scores > 3 | STARS: Finish with all 7 on the mat; Win within his first 3 raids\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 35/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 80/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him, but a Rusher standing NEXT to the kicked man charges the turned back — k = Kick held %, '(lands N)' = the Kick's landing chance); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Twist, one lesson — revival: two of your side are already out (5 on the mat). Every point you win brings one back, first out, first back, and a tackle is a point — so each stop is a man returning to the mat, each touch he lands sends another off. Only the two holds you know (no Block): his telegraph shows Hand or Toe, Thigh the Hand, Ankle the Toe, with the cover beside his target. Aha: defence is how you rebuild — two clean stops put all seven back. Stop 2 of his 4 raids and concede no more than 3; finishing with all 7 on the mat is the 3-star rebuild.","mechanics":["revival","ankle hold","thigh hold","cover position"],"optimal":4,"branching":7,"trap":0,"explored":600},{"n":20,"grid":"[Match · spike · Ch2 District Cup] OPP MAT: A o T B T o A · grip 0.70 · KEY: A ankle-catcher (Toe/hop/Dubki risky), o rookie, T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky), B blocker (Dash risky)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: alternate: 4 raids / 4 defences · start score 13-13 · empty raids 1/1\nMY MOVES: hand toe bonus walk dash dubki pull | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block hold\nCPU RAIDER \"District star\": s 0.49 · Easy · touches hand/toe/bonus · home walk/dash/dubki · up to 1 touch\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1A:h7/t34 2o:h24/t24 3T:h37/t11 4B:h37/t12 5T:h37/t11 6o:h24/t24 7A:h7/t34 bonus:43 | home after 1 touch: walk 43%, dash 39%, dubki 43% | after 2: walk 53%, dash 48%, dubki 53% | if held: pull 41%\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 20/thigh 52; toe: ankle 54/thigh 19; bonus: ankle 33/thigh 22 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 21/thigh 38/block 27; dash: ankle 34/thigh 18/block 52; dubki: ankle 39/thigh 6/block 9 | his touch lands 82% if untackled\nGOAL: win by 1+ | STARS: Win by 3; No empty raids\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 38/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 84/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him, but a Rusher standing NEXT to the kicked man charges the turned back — k = Kick held %, '(lands N)' = the Kick's landing chance); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Spike built only from chapter 2's verbs: level at 13-13, 4 raids each left. You are on 1 empty raid (one more patient raid is allowed, a second would make the third Do-or-Die), their raider takes one touch or hops the bonus. Ankle-catchers on the corners make your bonus hop a real risk (READ); the rookies in slots 2 and 6 are the safe touches, the T's beside the Blocker want the Toe. Aha: in a one-point game, count the empties — bank one safe Toe point early, then decide whether the bonus is worth its risk. Win by 1.","mechanics":["empty-raid counter","bonus line","toe touch","dubki","block (defensive wall)","ankle-catchers"],"optimal":null,"branching":18,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":21,"grid":"[Ghost Duel · breather · Ch2 District Cup] OPP MAT: o T o o o T o · grip 0.45 · KEY: o rookie, T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you raid 4x\nMY MOVES: hand toe bonus walk dash dubki pull\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1o:h15/t5 2T:h25/t7 3o:h16/t6 4o:h7/t6 5o:h16/t6 6T:h25/t7 7o:h15/t5 bonus:5 | home after 1 touch: walk 25%, dash 12%, dubki 9% | after 2: walk 32%, dash 16%, dubki 13% | if held: pull 44%\nGHOST REPLAY (on screen: before each of your raids the mat shows the ghost's SAME-numbered raid, its plan and result; ghost total 4): R1 Bonus → Toe #1 → Dubki: +2 | R2 Dubki: empty | R3 Toe #7 → Dubki → Pull free: +2 | R4 Toe #3 → Toe #6 → Toe #4 → Hand #5 → Walk: caught\nGOAL: beat the ghost's 4 points, 1x bonus | FAIL: raider out 2x | STARS: Earn 2 bonus points; Never get caught\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 38/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 85/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him, but a Rusher standing NEXT to the kicked man charges the turned back — k = Kick held %, '(lands N)' = the Kick's landing chance); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except 