the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Chapter boss with a Do-or-Die finish, kept to one session: the last 8 minutes of the District Final (~12 raids), one down at 16-17. A, T and B defenders and a raider who hops the bonus and Dubkis home; Do-or-Die is live on both sides, so the empty raids you spend early decide who is forced at the end. Aha: manage the empties like a clock — spend patience while level, never while behind. Win the match.","mechanics":["full match","do-or-die raid","bonus line","toe touch","dubki","block (defensive wall)","ankle-catchers","thigh-holders"],"optimal":null,"branching":18,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":23,"grid":"[Raid Puzzle · teach · Ch3 State League] OPP MAT: R o R o R o R · grip 0.73 · KEY: R rusher (touch/hop risky; Kick safe only with no R beside him), o rookie\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you raid 4x\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1R:h23/t22/k5(lands 92) 2o:h25/t24 3R:h25/t24/k7(lands 92) 4o:h25/t24 5R:h25/t24/k7(lands 92) 6o:h25/t24 7R:h23/t22/k5(lands 92) bonus:70 | home after 1 touch: walk 30%, dash 13%, dubki 28% | after 2: walk 38%, dash 17%, dubki 36% | if held: pull 45%\nGOAL: score 3, 2x kick | FAIL: raider out 2x | STARS: Win within 3 raids; Never get caught\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 39/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 78/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him, but a Rusher standing NEXT to the kicked man charges the turned back — k = Kick held %, '(lands N)' = the Kick's landing chance); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Teach the Backward Kick: Rushers (R) charge the raider and hold about a third of Hand or Toe Touches near them, but a Backward Kick tags a charging R at a fraction of that risk (READ). Aha: let the rusher come to you. Score 2 Kicks and 3 points in 4 raids.","mechanics":["backward kick","rusher defenders","hand touch","toe touch","dash home"],"optimal":null,"branching":22,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":24,"grid":"[Raid Puzzle · teach · Ch3 State League] OPP MAT: T T C C T T T · grip 0.36 · KEY: T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky), C chain link (walk/Dash risky when paired)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you raid 4x\nMY MOVES: hand walk dash pull lunge\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1T:h25 2T:h28 3C:h17 4C:h17 5T:h28 6T:h32 7T:h25 | home after 1 touch: walk 43%, dash 26% | after 2: walk 54%, dash 33% | if held: after 0/1/2 touches — pull 45/45/45%, lunge 62/45/28%\nGOAL: score 4 | FAIL: raider out 3x | STARS: Escape a hold; Score 5 points\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 33/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 79/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him, but a Rusher standing NEXT to the kicked man charges the turned back — k = Kick held %, '(lands N)' = the Kick's landing chance); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Teach ONE thing, the Escape lunge: no Toe, no Dubki, no Kick, no bonus — Thigh-holders and a chained pair (C C) will hold you, so you WILL be held, and the trial is about what you do then. The READ row lists both struggle gems by depth: the lunge for the line is the strong escape when held shallow (0 touches: lunge ~62% vs pull ~45%), they are level after one touch, and after two the lunge collapses (~28%) while the stamina pull-away stays ~45%. Aha: shallow → lunge, deep → pull — and that is why one touch per raid is the plan here, not three. Score 4 in 4 raids; caught 3 times and it's over.","mechanics":["escape lunge","struggle (pull-away)","chain links","thigh-holders","hand touch"],"optimal":null,"branching":9,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":25,"grid":"[Defend Stand · teach · Ch3 State League] OPP MAT: o o o o o o o · grip 1.00 · KEY: o rookie\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you defend 4 CPU raids\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush hold\nCPU RAIDER \"Bonus hunter\": s 0.45 · Easy · touches bonus/hand/toe · home walk/dash · up to 1 touch\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — bonus: ankle 34/thigh 23/rush 59; hand: ankle 21/thigh 54/rush 32; toe: ankle 56/thigh 20/rush 34 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 22/thigh 39/block 29/rush 17; dash: ankle 36/thigh 19/block 55/rush 12 | his touch lands 81% if untackled\nGOAL: stop 2 raids | FAIL: opp scores > 3 | STARS: Win within his first 3 raids; Concede at most 1\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 36/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 80/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him, but a Rusher standing NEXT to the kicked man charges the turned back — k = Kick held %, '(lands N)' = the Kick's landing chance); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Teach the defender Rush, and when NOT to use it: the state raider hops for the bonus line on about half his raids and Hand- or Toe-touches on the rest. A corner Rush is the best answer to a hop, but it is the worst answer to a touch — the holds stop touches (READ). So every raid is a read: hop → Rush, Hand → Thigh, Toe → Ankle. Aha: rush the hop, hold the touch. Stop 2 of 4 raids, concede no more than 3.","mechanics":["defender rush","bonus line","ankle hold","thigh hold"],"optimal":4,"branching":10,"trap":0,"explored":1083},{"n":26,"grid":"[Super Challenge · teach · Ch3 State League] OPP MAT: o o o o o o o · grip 1.00 · KEY: o rookie\nMY SIDE: o o - - - o - (3 on mat)\nFLOW: you defend 4 CPU raids\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush hold\nCPU RAIDER \"State raider\": s 0.44 · Medium · touches hand/toe · home walk/dash · up to 2 touches\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 21/thigh 54/rush 32; toe: ankle 56/thigh 20/rush 34 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 23/thigh 40/block 29/rush 17; dash: ankle 36/thigh 19/block 55/rush 12 | his touch lands 81% if untackled\nGOAL: 1x superTackle | FAIL: opp scores > 2 | STARS: Super Tackle within his first 2 raids; Concede at most 1\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 34/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 87/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him, but a Rusher standing NEXT to the kicked man charges the turned back — k = Kick held %, '(lands N)' = the Kick's landing chance); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Teach the Super Tackle: you have only 3 on the mat, so any tackle is worth 2 — but he goes for two touches, and lose all 3 and the all-out gives them +2. Choose WHICH of your three makes the tackle — the one beside his target (cover), never the man he touches. Aha: three defenders are a threat, not a weakness. Land a Super Tackle within 4 raids and concede no more than 2 (his two-touch raid can cost two at once).","mechanics":["super tackle","all-out","ankle hold","thigh hold","block (defensive wall)","defender rush"],"optimal":2,"branching":10,"trap":0,"explored":27},{"n":27,"grid":"[Raid Puzzle · twist · Ch3 State League] OPP MAT: R R o R o R R · grip 0.73 · KEY: R rusher (touch/hop risky; Kick safe only with no R beside him), o rookie · no scouting on this trial (no SCOUTED tags)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you raid 4x\nMY MOVES: hand kick walk dash pull lunge\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1R:h29/k18(lands 92) 2R:h32/k20(lands 92) 3o:h25 4R:h25/k7(lands 92) 5o:h25 6R:h32/k20(lands 92) 7R:h29/k18(lands 92) | home after 1 touch: walk 33%, dash 14% | after 2: walk 42%, dash 18% | if held: after 0/1/2 touches — pull 45/45/45%, lunge 62/45/28%\nGOAL: score 4, 2x kick | FAIL: raider out 2x | STARS: Score with 2 kicks; Never get caught\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 30/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 75/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him, but a Rusher standing NEXT to the kicked man charges the turned back — k = Kick held %, '(lands N)' = the Kick's landing chance); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Twist on the Kick (trial 23 taught: the Kick tags a charging Rusher). Now the Rushers stand in PAIRS — R R o R o R R — and a Rusher next to the kicked man charges your turned back (READ: Kick on a paired R ~18-20% held, Kick on the lone R in the middle ~7%, a Hand on a rookie between Rushers ~25%). No Toe, no scouting. And the mat changes as you score: every R you tag leaves, so the pair beside him becomes two lone Rushers for the next raid. Aha: kick the Rusher who stands ALONE — then break a pair so the next one stands alone too. Score 4 in 4 raids, at least 2 of them with a Kick.","mechanics":["backward kick","rusher defenders","hand touch"],"optimal":null,"branching":14,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":28,"grid":"[Super Challenge · teach · Ch3 State League] OPP MAT: o - T A - - o · grip 0.32 · KEY: o rookie, T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky), A ankle-catcher (Toe/hop/Dubki risky) · no scouting on this trial (no SCOUTED tags)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you raid 4x\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1o:h11/t3 3T:h18/t12 4A:h11/t18 7o:h4/t10 | home after 1 touch: walk 11%, dash 5%, dubki 12% | after 2: walk 15%, dash 7%, dubki 16% | if held: after 0/1/2 touches — pull 46/46/46%, lunge 62/45/28%\nGOAL: 1x allOut | FAIL: raider out 2x | STARS: All-out within 2 raids; Never get caught\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 38/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 79/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him, but a Rusher standing NEXT to the kicked man charges the turned back — k = Kick held %, '(lands N)' = the Kick's landing chance); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Teach the all-out: four are left — a rookie on each corner and a Thigh-holder beside an Ankle-catcher in the centre. Touch all four out and the all-out is +2 with their whole side coming back — but every point THEY win (a caught raid) revives one of theirs, so a greedy raid that gets caught undoes the work. The centre pair needs two different moves (Toe on the T, Hand on the A, READ) and each extra touch raises the next one's risk. No scouting on this drill. Aha: finish the job in the right order — the hard centre pair first while you are fresh, the corner rookies last, and never let a lone survivor revive them. Inflict the all-out within 4 raids.","mechanics":["all-out","hand touch","toe touch","dubki","thigh-holders","ankle-catchers"],"optimal":null,"branching":11,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":29,"grid":"[Defend Stand · twist · Ch3 State League] OPP MAT: o o o o o o o · grip 1.00 · KEY: o rookie\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you defend 5 CPU raids\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush hold\nCPU RAIDER \"State kicker\": s 0.55 · Easy · touches hand/kick · home walk/dash · up to 2 touches\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 19/thigh 50/rush 29; kick: ankle 17/thigh 21/rush 4 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 20/thigh 35/block 26/rush 15; dash: ankle 32/thigh 17/block 49/rush 11 | his touch lands 84% if untackled | Hold (step back) vs a real Kick: it finds nobody 65% of the time\nGOAL: stop 2 raids | FAIL: opp scores > 4 | STARS: Win within his first 3 raids; Concede at most 3\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 36/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 86/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him, but a Rusher standing NEXT to the kicked man charges the turned back — k = Kick held %, '(lands N)' = the Kick's landing chance); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Twist on the kick: now THEIR raider touches once and then Backward-Kicks the defender who chases him — his telegraph shows KICK before he turns, so you always see it coming. Chasing a kick is the trap (no hold catches it well, a Rush almost never). The counter is to step back: if nobody steps in (Hold), his kick finds nobody to tag 65% of the time, and his way home is still yours to Block. When he shows a Hand, Thigh Hold the touch as usual. The cost of the step-back: Hold never stops him on the touch, so the stop must come on his way home. Aha: never chase a kicker — step back, then beat his way home. Stop 2 of 5, concede no more than 4.","mechanics":["CPU backward kick","defender rush","thigh hold","ankle hold","block (defensive wall)"],"optimal":4,"branching":16,"trap":0,"explored":2141},{"n":30,"grid":"[Match · combine · Ch3 State League] OPP MAT: R T R B R T R · grip 0.72 · KEY: R rusher (touch/hop risky; Kick safe only with no R beside him), T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky), B blocker (Dash risky) · SCOUTED: a move from your last raid is tagged on its gem and ~6 pts more likely held (capped, same on every mat)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: alternate: 4 raids / 4 defences\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush hold\nCPU RAIDER \"