ck; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Combine chapter 3 with its one new idea, scouting: from here on state sides read you — the touch or way home you used on your PREVIOUS raid shows a SCOUTED tag and its % rises a few points (READ row). A mat of Rushers around a Blocker and two T's, and a raider with one plan — Hand Touch or bonus hop, then always the Dash. On your raids the rushers want the Kick and the wall wants the Dubki, so alternate Kick and Toe touches and never repeat the scouted gem; on his raids, Rush the hop and Block the Dash. Aha: the counter you used last raid is now the read one — switch. 4 raids each, win by 2.","mechanics":["defence reads repeats","backward kick","rusher defenders","blocker wall","dubki","defender rush","block (defensive wall)","bonus line"],"optimal":null,"branching":22,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":31,"grid":"[Revival Run · spike · Ch3 State League] OPP MAT: o T R o B T o · grip 0.95 · KEY: o rookie, T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky), R rusher (touch/hop risky; Kick safe only with no R beside him), B blocker (Dash risky) · SCOUTED: a move from your last raid is tagged on its gem and ~6 pts more likely held (capped, same on every mat)\nMY SIDE: - - o - o - o (3 on mat)\nFLOW: alternate raids 15:00→20:00 (~7 raids in all, ~4 each) · start score 5-9\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush hold\nCPU RAIDER \"State raider\": s 0.68 · Easy · touches hand/toe · home walk/dash · up to 1 touch\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1o:h29/t10 2T:h51/t22 3R:h45/t30/k12(lands 92) 4o:h25/t23 5B:h34/t15 6T:h46/t15 7o:h29/t10 bonus:31 | home after 1 touch: walk 53%, dash 48%, dubki 24% | after 2: walk 64%, dash 58%, dubki 31% | if held: after 0/1/2 touches — pull 38/38/38%, lunge 55/38/21%\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 17/thigh 45/rush 26; toe: ankle 46/thigh 16/rush 28 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 17/thigh 29/block 22/rush 13; dash: ankle 27/thigh 14/block 42/rush 9 | his touch lands 87% if untackled\nGOAL: finish within 2 | FAIL: trail by > 8 | STARS: Draw level; Land a Super Tackle\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 35/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 69/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him, but a Rusher standing NEXT to the kicked man charges the turned back — k = Kick held %, '(lands N)' = the Kick's landing chance); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Spike: all out at minute 5 — 5-9 down and only 3 back on the mat. Revival from trial 19 now runs a whole comeback: each point you score revives a team-mate (first out, first back), and with 3 or fewer every tackle is a Super Tackle. Aha: sacrifice greed for revivals — safe single touches rebuild the side. Reach 20:00 within 2 points; trail by 9 and it's over. A Super Tackle from three is the 3-star swing.","mechanics":["revival","all-out","super tackle","backward kick","escape lunge","dubki"],"optimal":null,"branching":19,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":32,"grid":"[Ghost Duel · breather · Ch3 State League] OPP MAT: o R o T o R o · grip 0.45 · KEY: o rookie, R rusher (touch/hop risky; Kick safe only with no R beside him), T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky) · no scouting on this trial (no SCOUTED tags)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you raid 4x\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1o:h10/t9 2R:h16/t15/k4(lands 92) 3o:h21/t11 4T:h25/t7 5o:h21/t11 6R:h16/t15/k4(lands 92) 7o:h10/t9 bonus:26 | home after 1 touch: walk 22%, dash 10%, dubki 14% | after 2: walk 29%, dash 14%, dubki 18% | if held: after 0/1/2 touches — pull 44/44/44%, lunge 61/44/27%\nGHOST REPLAY (on screen: before each of your raids the mat shows the ghost's SAME-numbered raid, its plan and result; ghost total 3): R1 Dash: empty | R2 Kick #2 → Dash → Pull free: +2 | R3 Kick #6 → Dash: +1 | R4 Toe #1 → Toe #7 → Toe #3 → Pull free: caught\nGOAL: beat the ghost's 3 points | FAIL: raider out 2x | STARS: Score with 2 Kicks; Never get caught\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 39/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 80/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him, but a Rusher standing NEXT to the kicked man charges the turned back — k = Kick held %, '(lands N)' = the Kick's landing chance); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Breather after the revival spike, and the chapter's Ghost Duel: your rival Sameer raided this friendly floodlight mat (rookies, two lone Rushers, one Thigh-holder, bonus line open), and the mat replays his run raid by raid before each of yours (GHOST REPLAY row: an empty Dash, two Kicks on the Rushers for +3, then a greedy Toe raid that got him caught). Beat his 3 in 4 raids — no defending. The toy: each Rusher stands alone, so his Kick is the safe point (READ ~4%). Aha: his replay shows where the points were (the Kicks) and where he wasted a raid (the empty Dash) — take both Kicks and a Toe on the T, and stop before the greedy third touch.","mechanics":["ghost duel","backward kick","rusher defenders","bonus line","toe touch"],"optimal":null,"branching":20,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":33,"grid":"[Full Match · boss · Ch3 State League] OPP MAT: R T B o B T R · grip 1.26 · KEY: R rusher (touch/hop risky; Kick safe only with no R beside him), T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky), B blocker (Dash risky), o rookie · no scouting on this trial (no SCOUTED tags)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: alternate raids 29:10→40:00 (~15 raids in all, ~8 each) · start score 11-12\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush hold\nCPU RAIDER \"State champion\": s 0.69 · Medium · touches hand/toe/bonus/kick · home walk/dash/dubki · up to 2 touches\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1R:h53/t35/k12(lands 92) 2T:h62/t30 3B:h42/t20 4o:h22/t19 5B:h42/t20 6T:h62/t30 7R:h53/t35/k12(lands 92) bonus:75 | home after 1 touch: walk 70%, dash 74%, dubki 36% | after 2: walk 80%, dash 84%, dubki 46% | if held: after 0/1/2 touches — pull 35/35/35%, lunge 51/34/17%\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 17/thigh 44/rush 26; toe: ankle 45/thigh 16/rush 27; bonus: ankle 27/thigh 18/rush 48; kick: ankle 15/thigh 18/rush 4 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 16/thigh 29/block 21/rush 12; dash: ankle 26/thigh 14/block 41/rush 9; dubki: ankle 30/thigh 5/block 7/rush 12 | his touch lands 87% if untackled | Hold (step back) vs a real Kick: it finds nobody 65% of the time\nGOAL: win by 1+ | STARS: Win by 3; Win by 6\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 35/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 69/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him, but a Rusher standing NEXT to the kicked man charges the turned back — k = Kick held %, '(lands N)' = the Kick's landing chance); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Chapter boss with a comeback, kept to one session: the last 11 minutes of the State Final (~15 raids), 11-12 down, no scouting. Full mat of Rushers, Blockers and T's; a raider who kicks chasers (step back) and hops the bonus (Rush the hop). Aha: one point back is a clean raid plus one stop — kick the rushers, Dubki the wall, and never chase his kick. Win the match.","mechanics":["full match","comeback","revival","super tackle","backward kick","escape lunge","defender rush","rusher defenders"],"optimal":null,"branching":20,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":34,"grid":"[Auction · teach · Ch4 Auction Hall] OPP MAT: o o o o o o o · grip 0.50 · KEY: o rookie\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: auction only\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush hold\nON SCREEN: purse helper (still needed + cheapest squad left)\nAUCTION (purse 72): Raider R8 open 35 market 45-60; Raider R6 open 12 market 14-22; Corner(ankle corner) open 12 market 14-24; Corner(thigh corner) open 10 market 12-20; Anchor(anchor) open 18 market 20-32; Anchor(anchor) open 14 market 16-26\nGOAL: buy Raider + Corner + Anchor | STARS: Keep 15 lakh in the purse; Keep 25 lakh in the purse\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 38/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 58/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him, but a Rusher standing NEXT to the kicked man charges the turned back — k = Kick held %, '(lands N)' = the Kick's landing chance); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Teach the auction: buy a Raider, a Corner and an Anchor with a 72-lakh purse. The star Raider Veer (reach 8) opens at 35 and the market values him 45-60; the second raider Kabir is a 14-22 bargain, the Corners 12-24 and the Anchors 16-32. Veer at even his lowest market price plus the cheapest Corner and Anchor is 73 — one lakh over the purse — so the star only fits if the room lets him go at the opening bid, and every lakh you raise for him is taken from the other two roles. The purse helper on screen shows the roles still needed and the cheapest legal squad left. Aha: a squad is three roles, not one star — bid for the shape first. Buy all three; keeping 15 / 25 lakh are the stars.","mechanics":["auction","player roles","purse"],"optimal":9,"branching":2,"trap":0,"explored":5288},{"n":35,"grid":"[Defend Stand · teach · Ch4 Auction Hall] OPP MAT: o o o o o o o · grip 1.00 · KEY: o rookie\nMY SIDE: A o o o o o T (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you defend 5 CPU raids\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush hold\nCPU RAIDER \"League raider\": s 0.38 · Easy · touches hand/toe · home walk/dash · up to 1 touch\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 22/thigh 57/rush 33; toe: ankle 59/thigh 21/rush 36 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 24/thigh 42/block 31/rush 18; dash: ankle 39/thigh 21/block 59/rush 13 | his touch lands 80% if untackled\nGOAL: stop 3 raids | FAIL: opp scores > 5 | STARS: Win within his first 4 raids; Concede at most 2\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 33/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 86/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-