assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Teach specialists: your left corner is an Ankle specialist (A, ankle ×1.25), your right corner a Thigh specialist (T, thigh ×1.25). The raider attacks anywhere with Hand or Toe. Aha: switch to the specialist whose hold matches his move when he is in range. Stop 3 of 5.","mechanics":["hold specialists","ankle hold","thigh hold","cover position","defender select"],"optimal":null,"branching":13,"trap":0,"explored":40000},{"n":36,"grid":"[Defend Stand · teach · Ch4 Auction Hall] OPP MAT: o o o o o o o · grip 1.00 · KEY: o rookie\nMY SIDE: A o o K o o T (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you defend 5 CPU raids\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush hold\nCPU RAIDER \"League raider\": s 0.25 · Easy · touches hand/toe · home walk/dash · up to 1 touch\nON SCREEN: Anchor range ring (±1 slot)\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 24/thigh 63/rush 37; toe: ankle 64/thigh 23/rush 39 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 28/thigh 48/block 35/rush 21; dash: ankle 44/thigh 24/block 66/rush 15 | his touch lands 76% if untackled\nGOAL: stop 3 raids | FAIL: opp scores > 5 | STARS: Win within his first 4 raids; Concede at most 2\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 36/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 89/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him, but a Rusher standing NEXT to the kicked man charges the turned back — k = Kick held %, '(lands N)' = the Kick's landing chance); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Teach the Anchor, with his range drawn on the mat: K in slot 4 multiplies every hold by 1.15 and his tackles rarely slip, and the shaded ring shows his range — slots 3-5, the target and one either side. Inside the ring the Anchor is the tackler whatever the move; outside it he is too far (half strength), so at the corners use the corner specialist when his hold matches the move, the defender beside the target when it does not. He never Dubkis home here (Walk or Dash only), so range is the only question. Aha: the specialists need the right read, the Anchor only needs the raider inside his ring. Stop 3 of 5.","mechanics":["anchor","hold specialists","ankle hold","thigh hold","block (defensive wall)"],"optimal":null,"branching":13,"trap":0,"explored":40000},{"n":37,"grid":"[Defend Stand · twist · Ch4 Auction Hall] OPP MAT: o o o o o o o · grip 1.00 · KEY: o rookie\nMY SIDE: A o o K o o T (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you defend 5 CPU raids\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush hold\nCPU RAIDER \"Feinting raider\": s 0.65 · Easy · touches hand/toe · home walk/dash/dubki · up to 1 touch · feints 30% · TELL on 60% of feints (telegraph flickers → it is a lie; a clean telegraph is true 85%)\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 18/thigh 46/rush 27; toe: ankle 47/thigh 17/rush 29 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 17/thigh 31/block 23/rush 13; dash: ankle 28/thigh 15/block 43/rush 10; dubki: ankle 31/thigh 5/block 8/rush 13 | his touch lands 86% if untackled\nGOAL: stop 2 raids | FAIL: opp scores > 5 | STARS: Win within his first 3 raids; Concede at most 3\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 37/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 88/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him, but a Rusher standing NEXT to the kicked man charges the turned back — k = Kick held %, '(lands N)' = the Kick's landing chance); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Twist: this raider feints — 3 raids in 10 the telegraphed move is not the real one — but feints have a tell: on 6 of 10 feints his hips turn first and the telegraph flickers (FEINT? on screen), so a flickering telegraph is a lie and a clean one is true about 85% of the time. Aha: trust a clean telegraph and counter it; against a flicker, use the all-round Anchor or an Ankle on his way home (it covers Dash and Dubki). Stop 2 of 5, concede no more than 5.","mechanics":["feints","anchor","hold specialists","block (defensive wall)","ankle hold","thigh hold"],"optimal":4,"branching":16,"trap":0,"explored":1537},{"n":38,"grid":"[Match · practise · Ch4 Auction Hall] OPP MAT: A T B o B T A · grip 0.85 · KEY: A ankle-catcher (Toe/hop/Dubki risky), T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky), B blocker (Dash risky), o rookie · SCOUTED: a move from your last raid is tagged on its gem and ~6 pts more likely held (capped, same on every mat)\nMY SIDE: A T o K o T A (7 on mat)\nFLOW: alternate: 4 raids / 4 defences · start score 20-19\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush hold\nCPU RAIDER \"League captain\": s 0.58 · Medium · touches hand/toe · home walk/dash · up to 1 touch\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1A:h25/t39 2T:h42/t29 3B:h31/t14 4o:h16/t13 5B:h31/t14 6T:h42/t29 7A:h25/t39 bonus:49 | home after 1 touch: walk 53%, dash 61%, dubki 50% | after 2: walk 64%, dash 72%, dubki 61% | if held: after 0/1/2 touches — pull 39/39/39%, lunge 56/39/22%\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 19/thigh 49/rush 28; toe: ankle 50/thigh 18/rush 30 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 19/thigh 33/block 25/rush 14; dash: ankle 31/thigh 16/block 47/rush 11 | his touch lands 85% if untackled\nGOAL: win by 1+ | FAIL: trail by > 1 | STARS: Win by 3; No empty raids\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 34/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 78/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends 