st move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Game management against a strong captain: you lead 20-19 with 4 raids each to go, and the trial is lost the moment you trail by more than 1. Your specialist squad defends (A corners, T covers, Anchor in the middle) against a Medium-thinking league captain who tests your specialists. A patient empty raid is safe while you lead, but two in a row make the third a Do-or-Die. Aha: protecting a lead is its own skill — bank the safe single touch, spend at most one empty raid, and tackle only with the specialist whose hold matches his move. Finish ahead, never more than 1 behind.","mechanics":["game management","empty-raid counter","hold specialists","anchor","alternating raids"],"optimal":null,"branching":10,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":39,"grid":"[Defend Stand · twist · Ch4 Auction Hall] OPP MAT: o o o o o o o · grip 1.00 · KEY: o rookie\nMY SIDE: A o T K T o A (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you defend 4 CPU raids\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush hold\nCPU RAIDER \"Two-touch raider\": s 0.64 · Medium · touches hand/toe · home walk/dash · up to 2 touches\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 15/thigh 58/rush 27; toe: ankle 40/thigh 21/rush 29 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 15/thigh 39/block 23/rush 13; dash: ankle 24/thigh 19/block 44/rush 10 | his touch lands 86% if untackled\nGOAL: stop 2 raids | FAIL: opp scores > 3 | STARS: Win within his first 3 raids; Concede at most 1\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 34/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 82/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, 