iled attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Twist: a two-touch raider — after the first touch he turns for a second defender, so the defender in range changes mid-raid. Switch to whoever covers the new target (the tap-select is instant). Aha: defend the raider's NEXT target, not the last one. Stop 2 of 4 and concede no more than 3.","mechanics":["defender switch","hold specialists","anchor","ankle hold","thigh hold","block (defensive wall)"],"optimal":4,"branching":13,"trap":0,"explored":986},{"n":40,"grid":"[Match · spike · Ch4 Auction Hall] OPP MAT: A T T o T T A · grip 1.08 · KEY: A ankle-catcher (Toe/hop/Dubki risky), T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky), o rookie · no scouting on this trial (no SCOUTED tags)\nMY SIDE: A T o K o T A (7 on mat)\nFLOW: alternate: 5 raids / 5 defences\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush hold\nCPU RAIDER \"League star\": s 0.65 · Medium · touches hand/toe · home walk/dash/dubki · up to 1 touch\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1A:h31/t47 2T:h60/t35 3T:h61/t15 4o:h49/t15 5T:h61/t15 6T:h60/t35 7A:h31/t47 bonus:58 | home after 1 touch: walk 70%, dash 36%, dubki 58% | after 2: walk 81%, dash 45%, dubki 69% | if held: after 0/1/2 touches — pull 37/37/37%, lunge 53/36/19%\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 18/thigh 46/rush 27; toe: ankle 47/thigh 17/rush 29 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 17/thigh 31/block 23/rush 13; dash: ankle 28/thigh 15/block 43/rush 10; dubki: ankle 31/thigh 5/block 8/rush 13 | his touch lands 86% if untackled\nGOAL: win by 1+ | STARS: Win by 3; Concede at most 2\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 35/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 79/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him, but a Rusher standing NEXT to the kicked man charges the turned back — k = Kick held %, '(lands N)' = the Kick's landing chance); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Spike on ONE layer, the specialist mirror (no Rushers, no wall, no feints, no scouting): your specialist squad (A corners, T covers, Anchor) against a league mat built the same way — A corners, four T's, a rookie in the centre — and a Medium raider who reads your shape. On your raids the counters are the chapter's two: Toe the T, Hand the A; on defence, match the specialist to his move and keep the Anchor central. Aha: both ends are the same lesson seen from each side — the hold that beats a move is the move that beats the hold. 5 raids each, win by 1.","mechanics":["hold specialists","anchor","ankle-catchers","thigh-holders"],"optimal":null,"branching":18,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":41,"grid":"[Auction · combine · Ch4 Auction Hall] OPP MAT: o o o o o o o · grip 1.00 · KEY: o rookie\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you defend 5 CPU raids\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush hold\nCPU RAIDER \"Toe specialist\": s 0.12 · Easy · touches toe/toe/hand · home dubki/dubki/walk · up to 1 touch\nON SCREEN: purse helper (still needed + cheapest squad left)\nAUCTION (purse 66): Anchor(anchor) open 16 market 18-30; Corner(thigh corner) open 8 market 10-18; Corner(ankle corner) open 28 market 32-44\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — toe: ankle 71/thigh 25/rush 43; toe: ankle 71/thigh 25/rush 43; hand: ankle 27/thigh 69/rush 40 | vs his way home — dubki: ankle 57/thigh 9/block 13/rush 24; dubki: ankle 57/thigh 9/block 13/rush 24; walk: ankle 31/thigh 55/block 39/rush 24 | his touch lands 73% if untackled\nGOAL: stop 2 raids, buy Corner + Anchor | FAIL: opp scores > 5 | STARS: Win within his first 3 raids; Keep 10 lakh in the purse\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 38/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 70/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him, but a Rusher standing NEXT to the kicked man charges the turned back — k = Kick held %, '(lands N)' = the Kick's landing chance); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Combine auction and defence, and the auction comes FIRST: the scouting report says their raider is a Toe-Touch specialist (2 raids in 3 a Toe, otherwise a Hand) who usually Dubkis home — both beaten by Ankle holds (READ: Ankle stops his Toe ~71% and his Dubki ~57%; the Thigh corner's holds stop them ~25% and ~9%). The Anchor is sold first (market 18-30), then the cheap Thigh Corner (10-18), and the Ankle Corner last — the room values him 32-44. The 66-lakh purse cannot pay the top of both markets (30 + 44 = 74), so what you pay for the Anchor decides whether you can still win the Ankle Corner. Aha: buy for the opponent you will face, not the bargain — and plan the last lot before you bid on the first. Buy a Corner and an Anchor, then stop 2 of his 5 raids.","mechanics":["auction","hold specialists","anchor","ankle hold","thigh hold","scouting"],"optimal":null,"branching":2,"trap":1,"explored":40000},{"n":42,"grid":"[Auction · twist · Ch4 Auction Hall] OPP MAT: o o o o o o o · grip 0.90 · KEY: o rookie\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: auction only\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush hold\nON SCREEN: purse helper (still needed + cheapest squad left)\nAUCTION (purse 75): Anchor(anchor) open 18 market 34-48; Raider R8 open 25 market 28-46; Corner(ankle corner) open 12 market 14-26; Raider R5 open 12 market 12-24; Anchor(anchor) open 15 market 18-30\nRIVAL BIDDER: Harbour Hawks chase the FIRST Anchor (+14 lakh on his value), then stop\nGOAL: buy Raider + Anchor | STARS: Keep 10 lakh in the purse; Keep 18 lakh in the purse\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 39/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 67/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him, but a Rusher standing NEXT to the kicked man charges the turned back — k = Kick held %, '(lands N)' = the Kick's landing chance); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Twist, auction only — read the other bidder: the Harbour Hawks need an Anchor and chase the FIRST one on the list, paying about 14 lakh over his market value (shown in the lot's market range); once they have one they stop. You need a Raider and an Anchor from 75 lakh, and the purse helper shows the sum on every bid. Aha: let the rival overpay for the first Anchor — his twin later goes at market, and that saving buys the better Raider.","mechanics":["auction","rival bidder","player roles","anchor","purse"],"optimal":9,"branching":2,"trap":0,"explored":4894},{"n":43,"grid":"[Super Challenge · breather · Ch4 Auction Hall] OPP MAT: A o o o o T A · grip 0.42 · KEY: A ankle-catcher (Toe/hop/Dubki risky), o rookie, T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky) · no scouting on this trial (no SCOUTED tags)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat) · raider reach 7 agi 6 spd 6\nFLOW: you raid 5x\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1A:h4/t21 2o:h6/t14 3o:h6/t5 4o:h6/t5 5o:h14/t6 6T:h22/t14 7A:h13/t21 bonus:27 | home after 1 touch: walk 19%, dash 9%, dubki 27% | after 2: walk 24%, dash 13%, dubki 35% | if held: after 0/1/2 touches — pull 49/49/49%, lunge 64/47/30%\nGOAL: score 4 | FAIL: raider out 2x | STARS: Land a bonus hop; Never get caught\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 38/40 (best 2★), a mid-skill player 85/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him, but a Rusher standing NEXT to the kicked man charges the turned back — k = Kick held %, '(lands N)' = the Kick's landing chance); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Breather with a show: Fans' Day on a friendly mat — five rookies, a Thigh-holder and Ankle-catchers on both corners — with your squad's raider (reach 7). The touches are easy (READ: Hand on a rookie ~6%, Hand on a corner A ~4%), so the crowd's request is the real choice: bonus hops. The corner A's make the hop the riskiest option on the mat (~27% held) and it is only live while six or more stand, and only the touches thin the mat — below six standing the hop is gone. Aha: a breather is where you try the show move — hop early while seven stand, score the safe touches after. Score 4 in 5 raids; a bonus hop with no catch is the 3-star show.","mechanics":["bonus line","ankle-catchers","thigh-holders","hand touch","score attack"],"optimal":null,"branching":18,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":44,"grid":"[Full Match · boss · Ch4 Auction Hall] OPP MAT: A T R B R T A · grip 1.31 · KEY: A ankle-catcher (Toe/hop/Dubki risky), T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky), R rusher (touch/hop risky; Kick safe only with no R beside him), B blocker (Dash risky) · SCOUTED: a move from your last raid is tagged on its gem and ~6 pts more likely held (capped, same on every mat)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat) · raider reach 7 agi 6 spd 6\nFLOW: alternate raids 00:00→10:00 (~14 raids in all, ~7 each, half-time swap at 05:00)\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush hold\nCPU RAIDER \"Franchise captain\": s 0.60 · Medium · touches hand/toe/bonus · home walk/dash/dubki · up to 2 touches · feints 15%\nAUCTION (purse 75): Raider R8 open 25 market 30-55; Corner(ankle corner) open 12 market 14-28; Anchor(anchor) open 18 market 20-36; Cover(cover) open 10 market 12-22; Corner(thigh corner) open 10 market 12-24; Anchor(anchor) open 15 market 16-30; Cover(cover) open 8 market 8-18\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1A:h35/t52 2T:h60/t46 3R:h55/t38/k17(lands 92) 4B:h42/t39 5R:h55/t38/k17(lands 92) 6T:h60/t46 7A:h35/t52 bonus:81 | home after 1 touch: walk 70%, dash 59%, dubki 69% | after 2: walk 80%, dash 70%, dubki 79% | if held: after 0/1/2 touches — pull 39/39/39%, lunge 53/36/19%\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 19/thigh 48/rush 28; toe: ankle 49/thigh 17/rush 30; bonus: ankle 30/thigh 20/rush 52 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 19/thigh 33/block 24/rush 14; dash: ankle 30/thigh 16/block 46/rush 10; dubki: ankle 34/thigh 6/block 8/rush 14 | his touch lands 85% if untackled\nGOAL: win by 1+, buy Corner | STARS: Win by 4; Win by 7\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 36/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 70/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him, but a Rusher standing NEXT to the kicked man charges the turned back — k = Kick held %, '(lands N)' = the Kick's landing chance); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting'