ntinental Cup] OPP MAT: o o o o o o o · grip 1.00 · KEY: o rookie\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you defend 4 CPU raids\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush chain hold\nCPU RAIDER \"Continental raider\": s 0.62 · Easy · touches hand/toe · home walk/dash · up to 1 touch\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 18/thigh 47/rush 27/chain 45; toe: ankle 48/thigh 17/rush 29/chain 41 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 18/thigh 32/block 24/rush 14/chain 44; dash: ankle 29/thigh 15/block 45/rush 10/chain 38 | his touch lands 86% if untackled\nGOAL: 1x chain | FAIL: opp scores > 2 | STARS: Chain him within his first 2 raids; Concede at most 1\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 36/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 79/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him, but a Rusher standing NEXT to the kicked man charges the turned back — k = Kick held %, '(lands N)' = the Kick's landing chance); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Teach the Chain Tackle: two adjacent defenders link. It is the one tackle with no wrong read — about as strong as the RIGHT hold on any touch (READ: chain ~45-49 vs the matching hold ~52-54, while the wrong hold is ~20), and the best stop of all on his walk home — but a broken chain costs two men, and the Dubki ducks under it. Aha: two defenders, one chain — when you are unsure of his move, chain the pair around his target; when you are sure, the matching hold is as good and risks one man. Land a chain tackle in his 4 raids and concede no more than 2 — one clean chain is the lesson, and a wrong pair costs a point.","mechanics":["chain tackle","ankle hold","thigh hold","block (defensive wall)","defender rush"],"optimal":2,"branching":18,"trap":0,"explored":63},{"n":47,"grid":"[Super Challenge · twist · Ch5 Continental Cup] OPP MAT: o o o o o o o · grip 1.00 · KEY: o rookie\nMY SIDE: o o C o C o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you defend 4 CPU raids\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush chain hold\nCPU RAIDER \"Greedy raider\": s 0.70 · Easy · touches hand/toe · home walk/dash · up to 3 touches · personality: goes for all 3 touches 40% of raids\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 17/thigh 44/rush 26/chain 47; toe: ankle 45/thigh 16/rush 27/chain 43 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 16/thigh 29/block 24/rush 12/chain 44; dash: ankle 26/thigh 14/block 45/rush 9/chain 38 | his touch lands 87% if untackled\nGOAL: stop 2 raids, 1x chain | FAIL: opp scores > 2 | STARS: Land 2 chain tackles; Concede at most 2\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 30/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 65/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him, but a Rusher standing NEXT to the kicked man charges the turned back — k = Kick held %, '(lands N)' = the Kick's landing chance); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Twist on the chain (trial 46 taught it as a stop on the touch): a full side of seven with two Cover men, against a greedy raider who strings up to THREE touches (4 raids in 10 he goes for all three). A tackle on his touch is a coin flip (READ: the best hold vs his touch ~44-47%), but every touch he makes slows him home, and the chain on his way home is your strongest stop (READ: chain vs his walk ~44%, the best of any tackle there). Aha: let a greedy raider go deep — then chain him on the way home. Stop 2 of his 4 raids, at least one with a chain, and concede no more than 2.","mechanics":["chain tackle","his raid depth","return tackle","ankle hold","thigh hold"],"optimal":4,"branching":11,"trap":0,"explored":1088},{"n":48,"grid":"[Raid Puzzle · teach · Ch5 Formation: Cage] OPP MAT: A C C o C C A · grip 0.54 · KEY: A ankle-catcher (Toe/hop/Dubki risky), C chain link (walk/Dash risky when paired), o rookie · SCOUTED: a move from your last raid is tagged on its gem and ~7 pts more likely held (capped, same on every mat)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you raid 5x\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1A:h8/t29 2C:h14/t23 3C:h14/t12 4o:h12/t11 5C:h14/t12 6C:h14/t23 7A:h8/t29 bonus:35 | home after 1 touch: walk 41%, dash 41%, dubki 35% | after 2: walk 51%, dash 51%, dubki 44% | if held: after 0/1/2 touches — pull 38/38/38%, lunge 54/37/20%\nGOAL: score 4 | FAIL: raider out 2x | STARS: Win within 4 raids; Never get caught\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 36/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 66/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him, but a Rusher standing NEXT to the kicked man charges the turned back — k = Kick held %, '(lands N)' = the Kick's landing chance); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Teach the Cage theme: two chained pairs (C C) shut the walk and the Dash home, and Ankle-catchers on both corners read the Dubki — so on the first raid all three ways home are close (READ: after a touch walk ~41%, Dash ~41%, Dubki ~35%). The Cage is beaten from the outside in: a Hand on a corner A is the safe touch (~8%), and every A you put out makes the Dubki under the chains cleaner, while every C you tag breaks his pair for the next raid. Scouting is on, so the same way home twice in a row is read. Aha: re-price the way home after every raid — open the corner, then duck under the Cage. Score 4 in 5 raids.","mechanics":["formation theme: Cage","chain links","dubki","toe touch","hand touch"],"optimal":null,"branching":18,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":49,"grid":"[Raid Puzzle · twist · Ch5 Formation: Pincer] OPP MAT: A R o B o R A · grip 0.15 · KEY: A ankle-catcher (Toe/hop/Dubki risky), R rusher (touch/hop risky; Kick safe only with no R beside him), o rookie, B blocker (Dash risky) · no scouting on this trial (no SCOUTED tags)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you raid 5x\nMY MOVES: hand toe bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1A:h3/t10 2R:h6/t9 3o:h4/t4 4B:h3/t3 5o:h4/t4 6R:h6/t9 7A:h3/t10 bonus:19 | home after 1 touch: walk 8%, dash 9%, dubki 13% | after 2: walk 10%, dash 12%, dubki 17% | if held: after 0/1/2 touches — pull 48/48/48%, lunge 65/48/31%\nGOAL: score 3, 1x bonus | FAIL: raider out 2x | STARS: Win within 4 raids; Never get caught\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 30/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 69/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him, but a Rusher standing NEXT to the kicked man charges the turned back — k = Kick held %, '(lands N)' = the Kick's landing chance); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Twist theme, the Pincer: Ankle-catcher corners and two Rushers just inside them close on the bonus line — the bonus hop is the riskiest option on this mat (READ: bonus ~19% held, every touch 3-10%), and it is REQUIRED: one bonus point is part of the goal. No Kick here, no scouting: the Rushers can only be read, not turned. And the bonus is live only while six stand, so the order matters. Aha: the squeeze is a timing puzzle — take the hop on an early raid while the line is full, then score the soft rookies and the Blocker in the middle. Score 3 in 5 raids including a bonus point.","mechanics":["formation theme: Pincer","ankle-catchers","rusher defenders","blocker","bonus line"],"optimal":null,"branching":18,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":50,"grid":"[Raid Puzzle · teach · Ch5 Continental Cup] OPP MAT: o o T o T o o · grip 1.05 · KEY: o rookie, T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky) · SCOUTED: a move from your last raid is tagged on its gem and ~7 pts more likely held (capped, same on every mat)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you raid 4x · DRS reviews 1\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1o:h12/t10 2o:h34/t14 3T:h48/t15 4o:h48/t15 5T:h48/t15 6o:h34/t14 7o:h12/t10 bonus:12 | home after 1 touch: walk 48%, dash 26%, dubki 21% | after 2: walk 59%, dash 33%, dubki 27% | if held: after 0/1/2 touches — pull 37/37/37%, lunge 53/36/19%\nGOAL: score 4 | FAIL: raider out 2x | STARS: Win a DRS review; Never get caught\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 35/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 70/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him, but a Rusher standing NEXT to the kicked man charges the turned back — k = Kick held %, '(lands N)' = the Kick's landing chance); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Teach DRS on an easy mat, so the review is the only lesson: rookies with two Thigh-holders. Close touches are called by the referee and the call says how close: 'very tight' calls are wrong almost half the time, 'tight' ones 1 in 5 — and until you use your first review every close call here comes up 'very tight' and wrong, so the lesson always comes up. You have 1 review and a failed review is lost. Aha: spend the one review on a very tight call, accept the merely tight ones — a review is a resource, not a reflex. Score 4 in 4 raids — one point a raid, so a wrong call you don't review costs the trial.","mechanics":["DRS review","toe touch","hand touch","dubki"],"optimal":null,"branching":18,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":51,"grid":"[Ghost Duel · twist · Ch5 Formation: Ghost Gate] OPP MAT: o o o o o o o · grip 1.00 · KEY: o rookie\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you defend 5 CPU raids\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush chain hold\nCPU RAIDER \"Ghost raider\": s 0.67 · Easy · touches hand/toe/bonus · home walk/dash/dubki · up to 2 touches · GHOST PLAN: toe@1>dash | hand@3>walk | bonus>walk | hand@5,toe@4>dubki | toe@0>dash\nON SCREEN: the ghost's next raid plan shown above the mat; the matching counter stops +15 pts (in the READ row)\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 17/thigh 56/rush 26/chain 43; toe: ankle 58/thigh 16/rush 28/chain 40; bonus: ankle 28/thigh 19/rush 60/chain 25 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 17/thigh 41/block 22/rush 13/chain 54; dash: ankle 27/thigh 14/block 55/rush 9/chain 36; dubki: ankle 42/thigh 5/block 7/rush 13/chain 11 | his touch lands 87% if untackled\nGOAL: stop 3 raids | FAIL: opp scores > 3 | STARS: Win within his first 4 raids; Land a chain tackle\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 27/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 70/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him, but a Rusher standing NEXT to the kicked man charges the turned back — k = Kick held %, '(lands N)' = the Kick's landing chance); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Twist: defend against a recorded ghost raider. Its 5 raids are known before you start (GHOST PLAN row: a Toe and Dash home, a Hand and walk, a bonus hop, a two-touch raid with a Dubki home, a corner Toe and Dash) and replay exactly — no feints — so the right counter is set up in advance and stops about 15 points more than usual (READ: Thigh v Hand, Ankle v Toe and Dubki, Rush v the hop, Block v the Dash, Chain v the walk). A chain tackle is the 3-star show but it costs two men if it breaks. Aha: a ghost can be solved: plan the perfect counter for each raid. Stop 3 of 5 and concede no more than 3.","mechanics":["ghost gate","chain tackle","block (defensive wall)","ankle hold","thigh hold","defender rush"],"optimal":null,"branching":15,"trap":0,"explored":40000},{"n":52,"grid":"[Match · combine · Ch5 Formation: Diamond] OPP MAT: o T R B R T o · grip 1.00 · KEY: o rookie, T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky), R rusher (touch/hop risky; Kick safe only with no R beside him), B blocker (Dash risky) · SCOUTED: a move from your last raid is tagged on its gem and ~7 pts more likely held (capped, same on every mat)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: alternate: 4 raids / 4 defences\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush chain hold\nCPU RAIDER \"Continental raider\": s 0.65 · Medium · touches hand/toe · home walk/dash · up to 2 touches\nON SCREEN: Blocker wall drawn on the midline; the Dash gem carries a WALLED tag with its real % (shown, never a hidden trap)\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1o:h30/t10 2T:h53/t23 3R:h48/t32/k14(lands 92) 4B:h36/t33 5R:h48/t32/k14(lands 92) 6T:h53/t23 7o:h30/t10 bonus:49 | home after 1 touch: walk 58%, dash 50%, dubki 30% | after 2: walk 69%, dash 61%, dubki 38% | if held: after 0/1/2 touches — pull 38/38/38%, lunge 54/37/20%\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 18/thigh 46/rush 27/chain 44; toe: ankle 47/thigh 17/rush 29/chain 40 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 18/thigh 31/block 23/rush 13/chain 42; dash: ankle 28/thigh 15/block 43/rush 10/chain 37 | his touch lands 86% if untackled\nGOAL: win by 2+ | STARS: Win by 4; Land a chain tackle\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 30/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 60/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him, but a Rusher standing NEXT to the kicked man charges the turned back — k = Kick held %, '(lands N)' = the Kick's landing chance); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"The Diamond theme as a lesson, not a slog: a Blocker at the point, Rushers on its shoulders, T's behind, rookie corners. Each layer has one answer — Kick the rushers, Toe the T's, Dubki under the wall's arms (the Dash is WALLED) — and the Medium raider strings two touches, so a chain around his NEXT target is your stop. No feints; the Diamond scouts you (SCOUTED tags), so vary the way home. Aha: a formation is read layer by layer: the point tells you the way home, the shoulders tell you the touch. 4 raids each, win by 2.","mechanics":["formation theme: Diamond","chain tackle","rusher defenders","blocker wall","thigh-holders","dubki"],"optimal":null,"branching":20,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":53,"grid":"[Ghost Duel · spike · Ch5 Formation: Cage] OPP MAT: T C C o C C T · grip 1.05 · KEY: T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky), C chain link (walk/Dash risky when paired), o rookie · SCOUTED: a move from your last raid is tagged on its gem and ~7 pts more likely held (capped, same on every mat)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you raid 5x\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1T:h48/t15 2C:h42/t23 3C:h25/t23 4o:h22/t20 5C:h25/t23 6C:h42/t23 7T:h48/t15 bonus:22 | home after 1 touch: walk 75%, dash 67%, dubki 21% | after 2: walk 84%, dash 78%, dubki 27% | if held: after 0/1/2 touches — pull 37/37/37%, lunge 53/36/19%\nGHOST REPLAY (on screen: before each of your raids the mat shows the ghost's SAME-numbered raid, its plan and result; ghost total 4): R1 Dubki: empty | R2 Bonus → Dubki → Lunge: +2 | R3 Dubki: empty | R4 Bonus → Dubki: +1 | R5 Bonus → Toe #7 → Pull free: caught\nGOAL: beat the ghost's 4 points | FAIL: raider out 3x | STARS: Dubki home twice; Never get caught\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 31/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 77/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him, but a Rusher standing NEXT to the kicked man charges the turned back — k = Kick held %, '(lands N)' = the Kick's landing chance); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Spike: this week's ladder ghost Ravi raided the Cage (two chained pairs, T's at the corners) 5 times and scored 4, and his run replays raid by raid on the mat (GHOST REPLAY row: two empty Dubkis, three bonus raids for +3, and he is caught on his last). Beat it (5+) in your 5 raids. The chains make every walk or Dash home a risk, so Dubki home like he did; his two empty raids are where you win — one point a raid leaves no room for a caught raid, so one raid should take a greedy second touch, and every touch makes the way home deeper (READ: home after 1 vs after 2). Aha: beat a ghost where he was idle — turn his empty raids into touches, on the rookie in slot 4 and his chain-link neighbour, then duck home.","mechanics":["ghost duel","formation theme: Cage","chain links","raid depth","dubki"],"optimal":null,"branching":18,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":54,"grid":"[Ghost Duel · breather · Ch5 Continental Cup] OPP MAT: o R o C C o o · grip 0.45 · KEY: o rookie, R rusher (touch/hop risky; Kick safe only with no R beside him), C chain link (walk/Dash risky when paired) · no scouting on this trial (no SCOUTED tags)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you raid 4x\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1o:h10/t9 2R:h16/t15/k4(lands 92) 3o:h13/t12 4C:h12/t10 5C:h12/t10 6o:h9/t8 7o:h5/t5 bonus:16 | home after 1 touch: walk 24%, dash 23%, dubki 11% | after 2: walk 31%, dash 29%, dubki 15% | if held: after 0/1/2 touches — pull 40/40/40%, lunge 56/39/22%\nGHOST REPLAY (on screen: before each of your raids the mat shows the ghost's SAME-numbered raid, its plan and result; ghost total 4): R1 Dubki → Lunge: +1 | R2 Bonus → Toe #1 → Dubki: +2 | R3 Toe #7 → Dubki: +1 | R4 Toe #3 → Toe #6 → Toe #4 → Hand #5 → Walk: caught\nGOAL: beat the ghost's 4 points | FAIL: raider out 2x | STARS: Land a bonus hop; Never get caught\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 36/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 79/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him, but a Rusher standing NEXT to the kicked man charges the turned back — k = Kick held %, '(lands N)' = the Kick's landing chance); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT?