 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Teach fatigue on a soft mat, so tiredness is the only thing you fight: rookies with two Thigh-holders and a gentle raider. Your star Veer (reach 8) tires fast (stamina 2); Kabir (reach 5, stamina 8) can go all day. A tired raider reaches less and is held more — watch the stamina % on the WHO RAIDS card. Aha: rotate — the star for the raids that matter, the workhorse in between. 5 raids each, win by 4 — a tired Veer on every raid will not get there.","mechanics":["fatigue","raider rotation","toe touch","hand touch","dubki"],"optimal":null,"branching":2,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":57,"grid":"[Raid Puzzle · teach · Ch6 World Championship] OPP MAT: - T A K A T - (captain weak to kick) · grip 0.66 · KEY: T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky), A ankle-catcher (Toe/hop/Dubki risky), K captain · no scouting on this trial (no SCOUTED tags)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you raid 5x\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 2T:h32/t21 3A:h31/t41 4K:h28/t47/k9(lands 66) 5A:h31/t41 6T:h32/t21 | home after 1 touch: walk 46%, dash 30%, dubki 49% | after 2: walk 57%, dash 39%, dubki 60% | if held: after 0/1/2 touches — pull 36/36/36%, lunge 53/36/19%\nGOAL: score 4 | FAIL: raider out 2x | STARS: Score with a kick on the captain; Never get caught\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 34/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 67/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him, but a Rusher standing NEXT to the kicked man charges the turned back — k = Kick held %, '(lands N)' 