him is dangerous and he guards every way home. His one weakness: he chases, so a Backward Kick on him is the safest touch on the mat (READ k on slot 4), and the kick tags him out of the way home too. No scouting in this lesson. Aha: kick the captain, don't avoid him. Score 4 in 5 raids.","mechanics":["rival captain","backward kick","ankle-catchers","thigh-holders","dubki"],"optimal":null,"branching":14,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":58,"grid":"[Defend Stand · teach · Ch6 World Championship] OPP MAT: o o o o o o o · grip 1.00 · KEY: o rookie\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you defend 6 CPU raids\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush chain hold\nCPU RAIDER \"The Dubki King\": s 0.54 · Medium · touches hand/kick · home dubki · up to 1 touch\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 20/thigh 50/rush 29/chain 47; kick: ankle 17/thigh 21/rush 4/chain 36 | vs his way home — dubki: ankle 36/thigh 6/block 9/rush 15/chain 13 | his touch lands 83% if untackled | Hold (step back) vs a real Kick: it finds nobody 65% of the time\nGOAL: stop 3 raids | FAIL: opp scores > 4 | STARS: Win within his first 4 raids; Concede at most 1\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 29/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 73/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him, but a Rusher standing NEXT to the kicked man charges the turned back — k = Kick held %, '(lands N)' = the Kick's landing chance); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Rival raider: the Dubki King always ducks home — under thighs, chains and walls — and only the Ankle Hold reads the dubki (READ). He knows you know: his touch is a Hand or a Backward Kick at whoever chases him, so the touch is a second read — Thigh the Hand, step back (Stay Back) from the Kick. Aha: a signature move is a promise — never chase the touch you can't win, and ankle him on the way home. Stop 3 of 6 and concede no more than 4.","mechanics":["rival raider signature","ankle hold","chain tackle","CPU backward kick","step back vs a kick"],"optimal":null,"branching":15,"trap":0,"explored":40000},{"n":59,"grid":"[Defend Stand · twist · Ch6 World Championship] OPP MAT: o o o o o o o · grip 1.00 · KEY: o rookie\nMY SIDE: o o C K C o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you defend 4 CPU raids\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush chain hold\nCPU RAIDER \"The Feint Master\": s 0.70 · Medium · touches hand · home walk/dash/dubki · up to 1 touch · feints 15% · TELL on 75% of feints (telegraph flickers → it is a lie; a clean telegraph is true 96%)\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 17/thigh 44/rush 26/chain 52 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 16/thigh 29/block 23/rush 12/chain 49; dash: ankle 26/thigh 14/block 45/rush 9/chain 42; dubki: ankle 29/thigh 5/block 8/rush 12/chain 13 | his touch lands 88% if untackled\nGOAL: stop 2 raids | FAIL: opp scores > 2 | STARS: Win within his first 3 raids; Land a chain tackle\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 30/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 59/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him, but a Rusher standing NEXT to the kicked man charges the turned back — k = Kick held %, '(lands N)' = the Kick's landing chance); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Twist on trial 37's feints — moved to the OTHER beat: the Feint Master only ever Hand Touches (his touch is always honest), but his WAY HOME is the lie: he shows Walk, Dash or Dubki and feints about 1 in 7, with a tell on 3 of 4 feints (the return telegraph flickers, FEINT? on screen). So the touch is the wrong moment to commit — Stay Back, let him take his one touch, and tackle on the way home: trust a clean return telegraph, and against a flicker use the Chain through your Anchor and two Covers, strong whichever way he really goes. Aha: in trial 37 you read his hands; here you read his feet. Stop 2 of his 4 raids, concede no more than 2.","mechanics":["return-beat feints","feint tell","chain tackle","anchor","ankle hold"],"optimal":4,"branching":15,"trap":0,"explored":2892},{"n":60,"grid":"[Match · combine · Ch6 World Championship] OPP MAT: R T o K o T R (captain weak to toe) · grip 1.31 · KEY: R rusher (touch/hop risky; Kick safe only with no R beside him), T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky), o rookie, K captain · no scouting on this trial (no SCOUTED tags)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat) · raiders Veer R8 A7 S7 st3, Kabir R6 A6 S5 st8, Dev R6 A7 S6 st6 (fatigue)\nFLOW: alternate raids 30:00→40:00 (~14 raids in all, ~7 each) · start score 16-18\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush chain hold\nCPU RAIDER \"World raider\": s 0.65 · Medium · touches hand/toe/bonus · home walk/dash/dubki · up to 2 touches · feints 15% · TELL on 50% of feints (telegraph flickers → it is a lie; a clean telegraph is true 92%)\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1R:h51/t33/k12(lands 92) 2T:h59/t27 3o:h49/t15 4K:h45/t13/k44(lands 70) 5o:h49/t15 6T:h59/t27 7R:h51/t33/k12(lands 92) bonus:73 | home after 1 touch: walk 74%, dash 50%, dubki 52% | after 2: walk 84%, dash 61%, dubki 63% | if held: after 0/1/2 touches — pull 38/38/38%, lunge 46/29/12%\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 18/thigh 46/rush 27/chain 44; toe: ankle 47/thigh 17/rush 29/chain 40; bonus: ankle 29/thigh 19/rush 50/chain 26 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 18/thigh 31/block 23/rush 13/chain 42; dash: ankle 28/thigh 15/block 43/rush 10/chain 37; dubki: ankle 32/thigh 5/block 8/rush 13/chain 11 | his touch lands 86% if untackled\nGOAL: win by 1+ | STARS: Win by 3; Never get caught\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 32/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 60/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him, but a Rusher standing NEXT to the kicked man charges the turned back — k = Kick held %, '(lands N)' = the Kick's landing chance); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Combine exactly two systems — fatigue and the rival captain (no scouting, no reversal): the last 10 minutes of a group match (~14 raids), 16-18 down, with three raiders to rotate (Veer the star with little stamina, two workhorses) against a mat anchored by a rival captain weak to the Toe Touch, rookies either side of him, Rushers on the corners. The captain's Toe is the safest point on the mat — but only a fresh raider reaches it reliably. Aha: spend the workhorses on the plain points and save Veer's stamina for the captain's Toe when the score is close. Win by 1.","mechanics":["fatigue","raider rotation","rival captain","toe touch","backward kick"],"optimal":null,"branching":3,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":61,"grid":"[Raid Puzzle · combine · Ch6 Formation: Cage] OPP MAT: o C C K T T o (captain weak to dash) · grip 0.98 · KEY: o rookie, C chain link (walk/Dash risky when paired), K captain, T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky) · SCOUTED: a move from your last raid is tagged on its gem and ~9 pts more likely held (capped, same on every mat)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you raid 6x\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1o:h14/t13 2C:h24/t21 3C:h36/t34 4K:h53/t40/k42(lands 66) 5T:h64/t28 6T:h57/t14 7o:h29/t10 bonus:11 | home after 1 touch: walk 71%, dash 49%, dubki 39% | after 2: walk 81%, dash 60%, dubki 49% | if held: after 0/1/2 touches — pull 30/30/30%, lunge 46/29/12%\nGOAL: score 4 | FAI