6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Combine: a half-Cage with a rival captain at its hinge — a chained pair on the left, the captain in the centre, two T's on the right. Two ways home compete (READ): the Dubki ducks under the chain and the T's but not the captain; the Dash is the captain's weakness (he cannot turn) but runs into the chain. And the answer moves: every chain link you put out breaks the chain for the next raid, so the Dash gets safer raid by raid. Aha: there is no fixed answer — re-price the way home after every raid. Score 4 in 6 raids; a Super Raid is the 3-star swing.","mechanics":["rival captain","formation theme: Cage","chain links","dubki","dash home","backward kick","super raid"],"optimal":null,"branching":19,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":62,"grid":"[Match · combine · Ch6 Formation: Wall] OPP MAT: B B o K o B B (captain weak to walk) · grip 1.30 · KEY: B blocker (Dash risky), o rookie, K captain · no scouting on this trial (no SCOUTED tags)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: alternate: 5 raids / 5 defences · start score 9-11\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush chain hold\nCPU RAIDER \"World raider\": s 0.65 · Medium · touches hand/toe · home walk/dash/dubki · up to 2 touches\nON SCREEN: Blocker wall drawn on the midline; the Dash gem carries a WALLED tag with its real % (shown, never a hidden trap)\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1B:h21/t18 2B:h25/t21 3o:h37/t35 4K:h48/t47/k47(la