elegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Combine the Wall theme with the rival captain, and the captain is weak to the WALK this time (trial 57's was the Kick): four Blockers make the Dash home hopeless (READ: Dash ~93% held, shown WALLED), so the way home is a real choice between the Dubki under their arms and the walk past a captain who can't turn (READ after a touch: walk ~53%, Dubki ~51%) — and it tips every raid as their men go out. Touch the Blockers on the outside (READ: Toe on an end B ~18%), never the captain (~47%); on defence his Medium raider strings two touches — chain the pair around his next target. 5 raids each from 9-11 down; win by 1.","mechanics":["formation theme: Wall","rival captain","blocker wall","defence reads repeats","chain tackle"],"optimal":null,"branching":19,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":63,"grid":"[Ghost Duel · breather · Ch6 World Championship] OPP MAT: o o o o o o o · grip 1.29 · KEY: o rookie\nMY SIDE: o o C K C o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you defend 4 CPU raids\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush chain hold\nCPU RAIDER \"Legend's ghost\": s 0.44 · Easy · touches hand/toe · home walk/dash/dubki · up to 2 touches · GHOST PLAN: hand@3,toe@4>dash | toe@2>dubki | hand@4,hand@5>dash | toe@3,hand@2>dubki\nON SCREEN: the ghost's next raid plan shown above the mat; the matching counter stops +15 pts (in the READ row)\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 21/thigh 67/rush 32/chain 61; toe: ankle 68/thigh 20/rush 34/chain 56 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 23/thigh 52/block 32/rush 17/chain 78; dash: ankle 36/thigh 19/block 74/rush 12/chain 56; dubki: ankle 53/thigh 7/block 11/rush 17/chain 17 | his touch lands 81% if untackled\nGOAL: 1x chain | FAIL: opp scores > 2 | STARS: Chain him within his first 2 raids; Concede nothing\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 38/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 84/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him, but a Rusher standing NEXT to the kicked man charges the turned back — k = Kick held %, '(lands N)' = the Kick's landing chance); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never 