ad — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Final boss, a mastery test of three things only, as a World Final Blitz of 2x5 game minutes from 0-0 (~14 raids): (1) their captain anchors a Pincer-Cage mat and is weak to the Kick — but his two Rushers flank him and charge a kicker's turned back (READ: Kick on K ~50% while both stand, Kick on a Rusher ~15%), so the captain's weakness opens only after you tag a Rusher out, (2) their raider is the Feint Master (1 feint in 5, three in four with the tell — the same read as trial 59), (3) you rotate three raiders through fatigue. No DRS, light scouting. Aha: the final asks for the chapter lessons in one match — tag a Rusher, then kick the captain, trust a clean telegraph and chain the pair around his target, save a fresh Veer for the closing raids. Win the match.","mechanics":["full match","rival captain","rival raider signature","feints","feint tell","fatigue","raider rotation","chain tackle"],"optimal":null,"branching":3,"trap":null,"explored":40000}]}
